content.text:
Now verify with a probe: load JoystickPad, check can_instantiate, and also scan ALL .gd files in the project for load failures (native-class collisions or other parse errors) — valuable because my earlier edits + potential other 4.7 collisions.

Write probe3.gd:
```gdscript
extends SceneTree
func _init():
	# 1) JoystickPad 是否能正常实例化
	var gd = load("res://scripts/mobile/VirtualJoystick.gd")
	print("P3 joystick_load=", gd, " can_inst=", gd.can_instantiate() if gd is GDScript else "n/a")
	if gd is GDScript:
		var j = gd.new()
		print("P3 has_move_vector=", "move_vector" in j, " value=", j.move_vector)
	# 2) 全项目脚本加载扫描
	var bad := []
	var stack := ["res://"]
	while stack.size() > 0:
		var d: String = stack.pop_back()
		var da := DirAccess.open(d)
		if da == null: continue
		da.list_dir_begin()
		var n := da.get_next()
		while n != "":
			var p: String = d.path_join(n) if d != "res://" else "res://" + n
			if da.current_is_dir():
				if not n.begins_with("."): stack.append(p)
			elif n.ends_with(".gd"):
				var s = load(p)
				if s is GDScript and not s.can_instantiate():
					bad.append(p)
				elif not (s is GDScript):
					bad.append(p + " (load_fail)")
			n = da.get_next()
		da.list_dir_end()
	print("P3 bad_scripts=", bad)
	quit()
```
Careful path join: `d.path_join(n)` works for "res://" too? `"res://".path_join("scripts")` → "res://scripts" probably fine. Simplify: use `d.path_join(n)` always.

Potential issue: bad scripts include `.cache`/`devprobe`? I skip hidden dirs (`.cache`), include devprobe (fine).

Scanning all .gd and loading: autoload-class scripts with `class_name`? Many will load fine. This may also load scripts with side effects? load() just compiles, no execution. OK.

Runtime: maybe 10-20s. Then kill after.

Also note: `load()` on a failing script prints errors to stderr → we capture and see all parse errors. 

Let me write and run.

