Now Minion._walk_opts must supply legs. Edit `_walk_opts`:

```
func _walk_opts() -> Dictionary:
	var base := {"stride": 1.15, "bob": 0.032, "sway": 0.04, "lean": 0.05, "dust_size": 0.18}
	if display_name in ["dragon", ...]: return {...}
	if display_name == "siege": return {...}
	base["legs"] = [visual.get_node_or_null("ModelPivot/LegL"), visual.get_node_or_null("ModelPivot/LegR")]
	return base
```
Careful `visual` may be unset when called from `_create_visual`? Called right after `visual = instance` set ✓ both branches set `visual` before attach? In the procedural branch: `visual = instance; _proc_visual=true; tint; WalkFeel.attach(self, instance, _walk_opts())` ✓.

But legs are children of `instance` (ModelPivot) ✓.

Also add "leg_swing": maybe 0.6 for normal, 0.5 for super (heavier).

Then turret stump in BattleManager. Find `func spawn_tower_wreck`.

