`AnimationPlayer.remove_animation` doesn't exist (it's on AnimationLibrary). So use the library: `ap.get_animation_library("")`? For glb-imported models, animations live in library "" (default) or named library. API: `AnimationPlayer.get_animation_library_list()`, `get_animation_library(name)`, `AnimationLibrary.remove_animation(name)` / `add_animation(name, anim)`.

Alternatively simpler approach without remove: since we cannot overwrite in place, we can instead **make the seated clip the only one used** by renaming existing clips to junk and adding seated clips under the standard names. Use library API:
```gdscript
var lib := ap.get_animation_library(&"")
```
For glb, animation player library name might be "" (default) — AnimationPlayer has a default library named "".

Implementation:
```gdscript
static func force_seated_anims(ap) -> void:
	var seat: Animation = ...
	var libs := ap.get_animation_library_list()
	for lib_name in libs:
		var lib: AnimationLibrary = ap.get_animation_library(lib_name)
		if lib == null: continue
		for nm in lib.get_animation_list():
			var key := str(nm)
			if key.begins_with("wheelchair"): continue
			var old := lib.get_animation(nm)
			var old_len := old.length if old != null else 0.25
			var src: Animation = seat
			var mapped := str(WC_ANIM_MAP.get(key, ""))
			if mapped != "" and lib.has_animation(mapped):
				src = lib.get_animation(mapped)
			var dup: Animation = src.duplicate()
			dup.length = maxf(old_len, 0.05)
			lib.remove_animation(nm)   # 交由 AnimationLibrary 处理
			lib.add_animation(nm, dup)
```
But `lib.get_animation_list()` returns Array[StringName]; iterating while modifying library — we call remove then add same name; safer to collect names first: `var names := []` then loop.

Also seat's animation object: it's in the library; duplicating gives independent Animation resource with tracks referencing paths — fine.

Careful: `ap.get_animation(name)` uses the *default* library; if glb puts everything in default library "" then ap.has_animation works ✓ (existing code uses ap.has_animation). So use default library: `ap.get_animation_library(ap.assigned_animation...` hmm. There's `AnimationPlayer.get_animation_library(name)`; default library name is `""`. Also `ap.get_animation(name)` resolves default library only. Let me just operate on the library returned by `ap.get_animation_library(&"")` if not null, else first library.

Also for 太乙真人's body male-f — has wheelchair anims? All character-* models presumably share the same animation set (32 anims incl wheelchair). Check: character-male-f anims earlier we didn't list; but male-c had them. Assume all share.

