content.text:
Manual target auto-clears when out of range/stealth ✓. But if the locked hero dies, is `manual_target` cleared? `manual_target.health > 0` condition means the clearing block skips dead targets → stale reference to dead hero remains; later `_nearest_skill_target` skips health<=0 but `_compute_skill_aim` uses `manual_target` → may aim at corpse position; also the picker button `.locked` compares to stale. Add clearing for dead target: extend L1796 condition to also clear when dead:

```gdscript
	if (not is_ai or net_taken) and manual_target and is_instance_valid(manual_target):
		if manual_target.health <= 0:
			manual_target = null
		elif global_position.distance_to(manual_target.global_position) > _aa_engage_reach():
			manual_target = null
```
This is a small robustness fix aligned with "锁敌头像" behavior (lock should drop on death). Do it.

Careful not to break `net_taken` semantics. Minimal edit.

