content.text:
RosterView is drawn from `rows` dictionaries. I can add vanguard info to header via rows data: e.g., in `_refresh_hero_detail_panel` pass extra info. But `set_rows(rows)` only takes rows. Simplest: add a field to the rows dict? Header sums rows; if I add a "vg" key on rows[0], header could read it. Hacky but minimal: add `set_meta`? Better: add optional param to `set_rows(r, md, extra)`. RosterView `set_rows(r: Array, md: String = "attr")` — add third param `info: Dictionary = {}` stored as `hud_info`, drawn in `_header()` as one line under the legend: e.g. "主宰先锋 我方 2 波 · 敌方 0 波" (gold if own>0, red if enemy>0, dim if none). Since header already has 3 lines, add to the legend line as appended text? Simpler: replace legend text position? Use extra line at y=76 right side: put vanguard text right-aligned at (PANEL_W-44-560, 76).

Implementation:
- RosterView: `var hud_info: Dictionary = {}`; `func set_rows(r: Array, md: String = "attr", info: Dictionary = {})` sets `hud_info = info`; in `_header()` after legend: 
```gdscript
	if not hud_info.is_empty():
		var vg_txt := str(hud_info.get("vanguard", ""))
		if vg_txt != "":
			UiKit.text(self, Vector2(PANEL_W - 44.0 - 620.0, 76.0), vg_txt, 21, Color(...), HORIZONTAL_ALIGNMENT_RIGHT, 620.0)
```
Color: pass from caller? Include "vanguard_color" in info dict.

- UI_Manager `_refresh_hero_detail_panel`: compute
```gdscript
	var my_w := battle.vanguard_waves_left(Config.player_team)
	var en_w := battle.vanguard_waves_left(Config.Team.ENEMY)
	var vname := battle.vanguard_wave_name()
	var vtxt := "%s 我方 %d 波 · 敌方 %d 波" % [vname, my_w, en_w]
	var vcol := UiKit.C_GOLD if my_w > 0 else (UiKit.C_DANGER if en_w > 0 else UiKit.C_TEXT_DIM)
	hero_detail_panel.set_rows(rows, "attr", {"vanguard": vtxt, "vanguard_color": vcol})
```
Hmm `set_rows(rows)` currently called with 1 arg; also other calls with mode? Check callers of set_rows and whether NetClientBattle also uses RosterView (client panel). Keep signature backward compatible.

- BattleManager helpers:
```gdscript
func vanguard_waves_left(team: int) -> int:
	if dominant_buff_team != team:
		return 0
	var left := dragon_minion_budget - dragon_count
	if left <= 0:
		return 0
	return int(ceil(float(left) / 3.0))

func vanguard_wave_name() -> String:
	return "风暴先锋" if dragon_minion_type == "storm" else ("暗影先锋" if dragon_minion_type == "shadow" else "主宰先锋")
```
Also expose "是否有主宰被击败" — if no one has killed dragon yet, dominant_buff_team=-1 and budget default 9; wave name meaningless. Show only when dominant_buff_team >= 0? Requirement says show after 主宰 defeated. If none: hide text (or show "主宰先锋 无"). I'll show only if `dominant_buff_team >= 0`, else "主宰先锋 未出动".

Now the damage popup color work:

Find `show_damage_number` in UI_Manager (L1059) and NetClientBattle L1330, plus NetSession.push_net_dmg.

